  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::477",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin appears to interact with Atp1a2 through a shared pathway involving Fxyd2 and potassium-transporting ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Acetyldigitoxin binds to Fxyd2, which then participates in potassium-transporting ATPase activity, ultimately leading to Atp1a2 being involved in this process. This indicates a potential mechanism where Acetyldigitoxin may modulate Atp1a2 through Fxyd2, possibly by influencing the activity of potassium transporters. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific nature of the interaction remains somewhat ambiguous. The overlapping roles of Fxyd2 in both potassium-transporting and sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase activities imply that Acetyldigitoxin may exert its effects through a common intermediary, potentially affecting Atp1a2 in a broader biological context.",
